    {
      "id": "rn_crVHckMJcJw7d56s::L2::Q8",
      "moduleId": "rn_crVHckMJcJw7d56s::L2",
      "stem": "Explain why the lens must be transparent and elastic at the same time.",
      "misconceptionClass": "design reasoning",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "Transparency lets light pass through undeflected except by its curvature, while elasticity lets the ciliary apparatus reshape it for accommodation; a lens lacking either property would either block the image or focus it at a fixed distance only.",
